   "short": false,
   "hook": "Korea's first hypersonic glide vehicle test",
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Welcome to Four Eyes Report. This week: Amazing K-defense. And then, an alphabet.",
     "audio": "audio/v3/new_001.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "amazing"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Amazing K-defense. That sounds like a movie trailer.",
     "audio": "audio/v3/new_002.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The numbers are real, though. In twenty twenty-five, Korea was the world's fourth-largest arms exporter, with about six percent of the global market.",
     "audio": "audio/v3/new_003.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "rank4"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Fourth in the world? That's higher than I guessed.",
     "audio": "audio/v3/new_004.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "And it's more than four times what Korea exported ten years ago. About twenty point eight trillion won last year.",
     "audio": "audio/v3/new_005.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "exports4x"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "And this week came a new chapter. Ms. Nonfic.",
     "audio": "audio/v3/new_006.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Good evening. On October eighth, South Korea test-launched its first hypersonic glide vehicle, or H G V, developed by the Agency for Defense Development.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_036.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "launch"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Hypersonic glide vehicle. That's three words I need explained.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_037.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Hypersonic means at least five times the speed of sound. Mach five. About six thousand one hundred kilometers an hour.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_038.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "mach5"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Wait. Don't ballistic missiles already go that fast?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_039.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Many do. The difference is the path. A ballistic missile flies a high arc, up and down, like a thrown ball. You can calculate where it lands.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_040.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "paths"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And the glider?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_041.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "paths"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "A rocket booster carries it high up. Then it separates and glides down through the atmosphere at lower altitude, and it can change direction.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_042.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "flight"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "A thrown ball versus a paper airplane. A very fast, very serious paper airplane.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_043.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "flight"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "I would not use the term paper airplane. But the physics is not wrong.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_044.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Why is that so hard to stop?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_045.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Three reasons. One: it flies low, and the curve of the Earth is in the way of ground radar, so it can be spotted later.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_046.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "low"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Two: missile defenses predict where a target will be, then aim there. If the target keeps changing course, the prediction keeps missing.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_047.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "course"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Three: less time. By the time it is seen, the window to respond can be a matter of minutes.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_048.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "time"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it's impossible to stop?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_049.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Nobody serious says impossible. They say difficult. I prefer accurate to dramatic.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_050.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And what's hard about building one?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_051.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Heat. At these speeds, friction with the air heats the surface far past a thousand degrees. It needs special heat-resistant materials.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_052.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "heat"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "And a communication problem. The heat can turn the air around the vehicle into plasma, which can block radio signals.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_053.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "plasma"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it's flying fast and can't call home.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_054.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "So what did Korea's test check? Officials listed flight path and speed, heat protection, guidance and control, and low-altitude maneuvering.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_055.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "checks"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "The presidential office says the vehicle separated from its booster, followed its planned path, adjusted course horizontally and vertically at low altitude, and hit its target.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_056.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "flight"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Speed and range were not disclosed. The site was not officially disclosed either. Yonhap reported a barge at a test center in Taean. That part is reported, not confirmed.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_057.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "\"Reported, not confirmed.\" That's Ms. Nonfic's love language.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_058.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "President Lee Jae Myung attended with the defense minister. He said the government will fully support the development and operational deployment of advanced weaponry.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_059.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "president"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "He also said the team must not rest on today's success, and that national security should rest on Korea's own strength.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_060.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "The same day, he inspected the Hyunmoo-5, a surface-to-surface missile nicknamed the monster missile. Officials used that name in a press statement for the first time.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_061.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "hyunmoo"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "The monster missile. The naming department had a good day.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_062.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "The timing matters. On October third, North Korea test-fired what Seoul assessed as a hypersonic medium-range ballistic missile. Seoul put its range at seven hundred kilometers. North Korea claimed one thousand.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_063.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "kmbars"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it's a race.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_064.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "I would not call it a race. I would call it a pattern.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_065.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Is Korea building anything else in this area?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_066.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Yes. HyCore. It is a different type: a hypersonic cruise missile. It keeps its engine running the whole way, using a scramjet. ADD and Hyundai Rotem have worked on it since twenty eighteen.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_067.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "compare"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Scramjet. What's that?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_068.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "An engine that burns fuel in air rushing past faster than sound. Think of keeping a candle lit in a hurricane.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_069.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "scramjet"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "In a twenty twenty-four test, HyCore passed Mach six at an altitude of twenty-three kilometers. The partners aim to begin mass production by twenty thirty-five.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_070.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "hycore_time"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Twenty thirty-five. So the future is nine years away.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_071.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "I will update the facts as they change. I do not update opinions. I do not have any.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_072.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
